        rules: {
          objective: 'Complete 6-color rainbows to collect cards, or have the most cards at the end.',
          gameplay: 'On your turn you play one card from your hand to the central Rainbow Line. The line builds toward a set of six different colors. If you play a card whose color is already in the line, or play a Cloud card, you must collect all cards currently in the line into your penalty pile. Wild cards can represent any color. The goal is to complete full rainbows to collect cards for points while minimizing penalty collections.',
          keyRules: [
            'Play one card per turn to the central Rainbow Line.',
            'Duplicate color or a Cloud in the line forces you to collect all cards from the line as a penalty.',
            'Complete six different colors in the line to form a Natural rainbow and collect those cards.',
            'Wild cards count as any color; hold Wilds for the 5th or 6th slot when possible.',
            'Winner has the most Natural rainbows or fewest penalty cards depending on variant.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Keep track of the line! If the line already has Red, Yellow, and Blue, DO NOT play your Red card. If you only have Red, you are forced to take the penalty. Try to hold onto your 'Wild' cards for the 5th or 6th spot in the lineâ€”this is when you are most likely to complete a rainbow and take the points.",
          intermediate: "Cloud Management: If the line has 4 cards in it, and you have a Cloud, use it! While it seems bad to take the cards, taking 4 cards is better than waiting and being forced to take 10 cards later. This is called 'Tactical Collection'â€”clearing the board so your opponent doesn't get a huge victory pile on the next move.",
          advanced: "The 'Spectrum Trap': If you hold most of one color (e.g., you have 5 Greens), play your Green card early. This makes it very difficult for your opponents to complete a rainbow because you are hogging the green cards. They will be forced to play a duplicate or a cloud, allowing you to reset the line on your terms.",
          tips: [
            "If you have a hand of all the same color, you're in troubleâ€”try to cycle your cards as fast as possible.",
            'A completed rainbow is worth 6 cards; a single penalty collection is often much more. Play for completion, not just shedding.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
